38. RELEASE DECISION RULES
====================================================

Possible final decisions:

GO — PRODUCTION READY.

CONDITIONAL GO — CONTROLLED RELEASE ONLY.

NO-GO — NOT PRODUCTION READY.

BLOCKED — CANNOT VERIFY.

GO IS PERMITTED ONLY WHEN:

All mandatory release gates pass.

No unresolved P0 defects exist.

No unresolved release-blocking
P1 defects exist.

Critical scientific tests pass.

Official progression is secure.

Core browser journeys work.

No critical GPU or camera defect remains.

Production configuration is valid.

Monitoring and rollback are prepared.

Mandatory test evidence exists.

CONDITIONAL GO:

May be recommended only if
noncritical limitations are clearly
documented and a controlled rollout
is supported.

NO-GO:

Use when known critical defects remain.

BLOCKED:

Use when required tests
could not be executed.

Never mark BLOCKED as GO.

